{{/*
  The theme's <head>. It overrides partials/document.gohtml, so both layouts get it
  and there is one copy of the two htmx settings rather than two.

  Two changes from the default: the Rivers mark as the favicon, and three stylesheets
  linked after the bundled one. Everything else here is the default verbatim, including
  the two htmx settings, which are load-bearing — see the comments.

  The stylesheet order is the theme. styles.css is the bundled sheet, unshadowed, so it
  keeps receiving upstream fixes; rivers.css is the whole of what Rivers changes and has
  to come after it to win. Reordering these two links breaks the theme silently — the
  page still renders, in the default's colours.

  helvetica.css is deliberately *not* linked. It cannot work as the files stand: the
  faces are .woff, which is not in static.go's contentTypes, and they sit in a
  helveticaneue/ subdirectory, which the STATIC_DIR walk skips outright. Linking it
  would buy eleven 404s and the same fallback the page already gets. See theme/README.
*/}}
{{define "document_head"}}<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
{{/*
  Through {{asset}} rather than a bare path: it resolves against STATIC_DIR, carries
  the file's content hash so a replaced mark is a different URL, and is absolute —
  a relative "static/R_White.png" resolves against /products/some-slug on a product
  page and 404s there.
*/}}
<link rel="icon" href="{{asset "R_White.png"}}" type="image/png">
<title>{{.Title}} — {{.StoreName}}</title>
{{/*
  Two settings, both load-bearing. Keep them if you edit this file.

  includeIndicatorStyles:false — htmx injects a <style> block for the indicator
  classes as soon as it loads, and style-src 'self' blocks it. Silently, apart from
  a console warning, and it fails *open*: the rule that hides an hx-indicator never
  applies, leaving a spinner permanently visible. So the injection is off and the
  bundled styles.css carries those rules instead — which is one reason this theme links
  that sheet rather than replacing it.

  responseHandling — htmx's default is to swap 2xx and to swap *nothing* on 4xx or
  5xx, which silently throws away every refusal this store sends: the cart answers
  "That option is sold out." as a 409 carrying the fragment meant for the page.
*/}}
<meta name="htmx-config" content='{"includeIndicatorStyles":false,
  "responseHandling":[{"code":"204","swap":false},
                      {"code":"[23]..","swap":true},
                      {"code":"[45]..","swap":true,"error":true}]}'>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{asset "styles.css"}}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{asset "rivers.css"}}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{asset "webflow.css"}}">
{{with .FontCSSURL}}<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{.}}">{{end}}
<script src="{{asset "htmx.min.js"}}" defer></script>
</head>
{{end}}
